course: dictionary
lesson: 1829
title: The coastguard
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The coastguard is an organisation that watches the sea near the coast. When people or boats are in danger, it comes to rescue them. Read the words around it to find its meaning. «Call the coastguard» tells you it is a service you can ask for when you are in trouble.
explain: Look at this sentence: «At the coast, call 999 and ask for the Coastguard.» The words around it tell you that the Coastguard is the help you ask for when people are in danger at sea. Ask yourself: who would come to rescue a boat in trouble? That is the coastguard. Then put your meaning into the sentence to check it.
explain: Sometimes a word is used for a person, not just a group. «A coastguard helicopter» flew over the waves, so the coastguard can also mean the helicopters and boats that do the rescuing. In a story, seeing a coastguard tells the reader that help is coming.
fact: The coastguard is an organisation that watches the sea near a coast and rescues people and boats in danger.
fact: A coastguard is also a person who works for this organisation.
fact: In the UK and Ireland, call 999 or 112 in an emergency and ask for the Coastguard if you are at the coast.
fact: In the US and Canada the emergency number is 911, in Australia it is 000, and in New Zealand it is 111.
fact: If you are cut off by a rising tide, call the coastguard. Never try to wade out through the water yourself.
exercise: «Call 999 at the coast and ask for the Coastguard.» What does the Coastguard do? | It makes the tide come in | *It watches the sea and rescues people and boats in danger | It builds sandcastles for children | It sells ice cream on the beach
exercise: «On some flat beaches the sea comes back in faster than you can walk; if cut off, call the coastguard rather than try to wade.» Why is the coastguard the right help here? | *Because they rescue people who are cut off by the sea | Because wading is the fastest way home | Because the sea is always calm there | Because they only teach swimming lessons
exercise: In the UK, which number do you ring at the coast to ask for the Coastguard? | *999 | 000 | 111 | 911
test: «The coastguard helicopter flew low over the waves.» What does this sentence tell the reader? | *Help is on its way to people in danger at sea | The sea is closed for a swim forever | The helicopter is going to a picnic | Someone has lost their shopping in town
test: Tyler asks, «Who do I call if my friend is cut off by the tide?» What is the answer? | A librarian, to find a book | *The coastguard, by calling 999 in the UK | A baker, to bring bread | The ice cream van driver
exam: In the US and Canada, which number would you call in an emergency at sea? | 999 | *911 | 111 | 000
